=====================================================================
 1. THRESHOLD -- binCV cuda::threshold vs cv::cuda::threshold
=====================================================================
 ROLE: 'turn a wide frame into a per-pixel above/below map on device'.
 Both sides are ONE launch. They differ in what they emit: OpenCV
 writes one BYTE per pixel (CV_8UC1, THRESH_BINARY), binCV writes one
 BIT. That difference is the whole point of the library and it is
 stated at the number rather than folded into it -- the outputs are
 not the same array, so this is a role comparison, not an equality.

