=====================================================================
 10. goodFeaturesToTrack -- binCV device-resident selection vs
     cv::cuda::createGoodFeaturesToTrackDetector (cudaimgproc)
=====================================================================
 WALL CLOCK ON BOTH SIDES, and the reason is on OpenCV's side: at
 minDistance >= 1 its detect() DOWNLOADS the sorted candidate list,
 runs the spacing filter on the HOST and uploads the survivors
 (cudaimgproc/src/gftt.cpp). A CUDA-event clock would exclude that
 pass and flatter OpenCV. binCV's selection never leaves the device.
 THE SPEED BAR FOR THIS OP WAS NOT WRITABLE -- its author escalated
 it rather than deriving a number from a host CPU ratio, and this
