=====================================================================
 6. NO BAR EXISTS -- verdict OUTSTANDING (owner ruling R2)
=====================================================================
 These ops have NO cv::cuda counterpart at any API level. Under R2
 they ship on correctness + memory + the host comparison, with the
 GPU speed verdict recorded explicitly as OUTSTANDING against the
 resident pipeline that will later price them. No substitute bar is
 invented here and no CPU number is quoted as a GPU bar.

   cuda::binarize     N-plane bit-sliced source -> bits. OpenCV has
                      no N-bit image type on host or device, so there
                      is nothing to compare the input side against.
                      SPEED VERDICT: OUTSTANDING.
   cuda::shift        integer translation of a packed bit plane. The
                      byte side's actual alternative is a pitched DMA
                      (cudaMemcpy2D), not a kernel -- timed below as
                      a reference, not as a bar, because binCV's one
                      funnel-shift instruction is being compared
                      against ZERO instructions on a copy engine.
                      SPEED VERDICT: OUTSTANDING.
   cuda::pyrDownBox   the N-bit rung itself (the LADDER has a role
                      bar above; the per-rung N-bit requantize does
                      not). SPEED VERDICT: OUTSTANDING.

