=====================================================================
 12. DESCRIBE -- binCV cuda::computeBriefSteered vs
     cv::cuda::ORB::computeAsync on PROVIDED keypoints
=====================================================================
 computeAsync IS accepted in OpenCV 4.5.4 on provided keypoints, so a
 stage-isolated GPU denominator exists and no differential is needed.
 SUPERSET vs SUBSET, stated at the number: computeAsync also builds
 ORB's level-0 pyramid entry and can blur. nlevels = 1 and
 blurForDescriptor = false pin that superset as small as the API
 allows; it is not zero, and the ratio is an upper bound on binCV's
 advantage for that reason.
 Both sides sample the SAME 256 pairs -- cv::ORB's learned table,
 which binCV reaches by pointer out of ops/orbPattern.hpp.

