=====================================================================
 15. CENSUS DENSE DISPARITY -- binCV's census entry vs
     cv::cuda::StereoBM, RE-TAKEN after the matcher changed
=====================================================================
 ROLE: 'a dense disparity map from a rectified wide-input pair,
 resident on device'. Section 7 runs the BINARY path, which is
 where this library's structural claim lives. This section runs the
 CENSUS path, which is the entry a wide-input caller meets first and
 where binCV has NO structural advantage -- census EXPANDS data,
 8 bits per pixel in and 24 out, and the layout that makes it fast
 is the conventional one-word-per-pixel descriptor.

 WHY RE-TAKEN. The packed census matcher was replaced this round by
 a warp-cooperative separable box arm, and the shipped report's
 census rows predate it. Three rows are printed: the matcher alone,
 the whole entry (two transforms plus the match, which is what a
 caller pays), and the arm's own off-switch ratio inside THIS
 protocol so the family's 2.4-2.5x is reproduced or contradicted
 here rather than quoted from another process.
 Both sides on one explicit stream: StereoBM calls
 cudaDeviceSynchronize() on the null stream in each of its three
