=====================================================================
 2. MORPHOLOGY -- binCV cuda::erode / morphologyEx vs
    cv::cuda::createMorphologyFilter (cudafilters, NPP-backed)
=====================================================================
 ROLE: 'erode / open a binary-valued image on device'. OpenCV's
 operand is CV_8UC1 with values 0 and 255; binCV's is one bit per
 pixel. Same operation, same element, same border, different
 representation -- which is the comparison this library exists to
 make. The filter object is built ONCE outside the timed region on
 both sides, as a caller would; only apply() is timed.
 BORDER: cv::cuda's morphology filter is BORDER_CONSTANT only, so
 binCV runs BORDER_CONSTANT here too -- the four border types binCV
 makes word-parallel have no counterpart on this side to be timed
 against, and are priced in cuda_window_benchmark instead.

