=====================================================================
 5. EDGE THRESHOLD -- binCV cuda::edgeThreshold vs the composed
    cv::cuda spelling (createDerivFilter x2 + abs + add + threshold)
=====================================================================
 ROLE: 'central-difference gradient magnitude, thresholded, on
 device'. There is no single cv::cuda call for it, so the bar is the
 composed spelling a caller would actually write. createDerivFilter
 at ksize=1 with normalize=false gives getDerivKernels' exact
 [-1,0,1] -- the same computation -- and defaults to
 BORDER_REFLECT_101, which is binCV's border here.
 createLinearFilter cannot be used: it asserts dst depth == src
 depth, and a signed derivative of CV_8U needs CV_16S.
 The chain is separable, so it is SEVERAL launches against binCV's
 one, and the launch count is derived from the API's structure --
 no profiler runs on this host to count them directly.

