=====================================================================
 11. CORNER RESPONSE -- binCV cuda::cornerMinEigenValAsync vs
     cv::cuda::createMinEigenValCorner AND createHarrisCorner
=====================================================================
 TWO DENOMINATORS, AND THEY ARE NOT INTERCHANGEABLE. binCV's op
 computes the MINIMUM EIGENVALUE of the gradient covariance, so
 createMinEigenValCorner is the like-for-like counterpart and is the
 bar. createHarrisCorner computes a DIFFERENT response (det - k*tr^2)
 over the same covariance and is timed beside it as context -- the
 task named it, and the honest thing is to run it and say plainly
 that it answers a different question, not to quietly substitute it
 for the one that matches.
 BOTH OpenCV arms read the CV_8U picture and internally run a Sobel;
 binCV reads four TERNARY BIT PLANES that already exist in the
 pipeline. That is a role comparison, not an equality, and the
 asymmetry is stated rather than folded into the ratio.

