=====================================================================
 4. PYRAMID -- binCV cuda::buildPyramidBox vs 3x cv::cuda::resize
    (INTER_AREA, 0.5) and 3x cv::cuda::pyrDown (cudawarping)
=====================================================================
 ROLE: 'build a three-rung half-resolution ladder on device'.
 cv::cuda::resize at INTER_AREA and scale 0.5 is the SAME FILTER as
 binCV's box -- a 2x2 average -- so that is the like-for-like arm.
 cv::cuda::pyrDown is a Gaussian 5x5 and is a DIFFERENT operation;
 it is carried because it is what a caller reaches for, and it is
 labelled as a different filter rather than quoted as the bar.
 binCV's ladder is N-BIT per rung (1,3,4,5) -- OpenCV has no N-bit
 image type, so the output arrays are not the same thing and this
 is a role comparison.
 ODD WIDTHS ARE NOT COMPARABLE: at width 753, resize's dsize is 376
 where pyrDownWidth(753) is 377. 752 is even at every rung, which is
 why the ladder is taken there.

